1
00:01:38,799 --> 00:01:39,400
Huadong.

2
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:40,359
Here.

3
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,840
Evaluate yourself.

4
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,040
I have a strong learning ability,

5
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:44,040
strong comprehension skills,

6
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,239
excellent exam skills,

7
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,920
and my work ability won't be bad either.

8
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,079
I think I'll choose him instead.

9
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:51,799
What was his name? Chun-something?

10
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,200
Chunxiao.

11
00:01:56,799 --> 00:01:58,120
Was there a problem with my answer?

12
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,560
Do I have to choose you just because there isn't one?

13
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:02,200
Of course, it's not your problem either.

14
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:03,879
An outstanding student like you,

15
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,359
Single-subject Gaokao top scorer, top student,

16
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,280
and all that.

17
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,840
You've won a ton of academic championships.

18
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,759
You're shining so bright,

19
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,039
the light is bursting out of this room.

20
00:02:11,439 --> 00:02:12,159
How outstanding you are,

21
00:02:12,159 --> 00:02:13,159
everyone can see.

22
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,560
But what suits you best

23
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,159
isn't intelligence work.

24
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:17,039
It's making arrests.

25
00:02:17,759 --> 00:02:18,439
To put it plainly,

26
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,479
How can someone with only a high IQ

27
00:02:19,479 --> 00:02:21,080
handle intelligence work?

28
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,479
Take him, for instance,

29
00:02:22,479 --> 00:02:23,400
with his delicate skin,

30
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,520
when we need to show up and intimidate,

31
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,439
he can put on a police uniform to make arrests,

32
00:02:25,439 --> 00:02:26,360
and throw his weight around.

33
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,319
Or he could give an internal report,

34
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:29,599
give a speech at the provincial department,

35
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:30,919
and present the outstanding deeds of others.

36
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:31,919
That would be perfect.

37
00:02:31,919 --> 00:02:33,639
Our national security system needs a face, too.

38
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,479
We can't all look like...

39
00:02:36,479 --> 00:02:38,479
look as busted as Brother Shan here.

40
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:40,159
What are you laughing at?

41
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:41,120
How do I know without trying?

42
00:02:44,479 --> 00:02:45,919
I don't think my IQ is low.

43
00:02:47,319 --> 00:02:49,520
It's precisely because your IQ is too high, brother.

44
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,080
Intelligence work requires more than just that.

45
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,639
More importantly, it requires emotional intelligence.

46
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,159
Someone like you,

47
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:56,840
grew up being praised,

48
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,039
surrounded by applause your whole life.

49
00:02:58,039 --> 00:02:59,360
Do you know how to read the room?

50
00:02:59,439 --> 00:03:00,919
You'd want to kill yourself over a few harsh words.

51
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:02,960
How could you go out, read people, and make friends?

52
00:03:04,319 --> 00:03:05,080
Let alone anything else,

53
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,039
if you go to the alley entrance,

54
00:03:06,039 --> 00:03:07,759
and look at a hundred random people on the street,

55
00:03:07,759 --> 00:03:08,919
who is truly wealthy?

56
00:03:09,039 --> 00:03:10,000
Who is pretending to be wealthy?

57
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,159
Who is harboring malicious thoughts?

58
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:12,080
could you figure it out?

59
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,879
Just like earlier,

60
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,800
you couldn't even tell a lie.

61
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:17,400
You really won't do.

62
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,240
Can Chunxiao lie, then?

63
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:21,719
He's even worse at it.

64
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,280
But he's not as outstanding as you,

65
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,280
not as good-looking as you,

66
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,400
and not as smart as you.

67
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,840
At least, on the outside,

68
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,159
he still looks like an ordinary guy.

69
00:03:28,159 --> 00:03:29,800
Thrown into a crowd on the street,

70
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,080
he wouldn't be easily recognized.

71
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,479
Why else would I choose him?

72
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,479
Chunxiao, what are you waiting for?

73
00:03:38,479 --> 00:03:39,479
Go follow your mentor.

74
00:03:41,599 --> 00:03:43,680
Wu Jiali, Huadong is yours.

75
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,879
Welcome to Minzhong, everyone.

76
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,840
Boss Wen's friends

77
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,960
are my good friends.

78
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:51,199
From now on, you are all my brothers and sisters.

79
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,080
I'll be at your service from now on.

80
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,479
Bottoms up. Bottoms up.

81
00:03:54,879 --> 00:03:55,360
Thank you, Chief Wu.

82
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:55,960
Great, great, great.

83
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,599
Thank you.

84
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:03,759
Boss Ding.

85
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,400
Wo Aoma

86
00:04:05,599 --> 00:04:07,680
is a massive supermarket, a large enterprise,

87
00:04:07,759 --> 00:04:08,800
a huge corporation.

88
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,360
The attitude I've shown here

89
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,319
has been completely sincere.

90
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,400
Boss Wen knows my character.

91
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,400
Isn't that right, Boss Wen?

92
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,480
Excuse me.

93
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,439
Okay, okay.

94
00:04:22,279 --> 00:04:23,480
Excuse me, please make way.

95
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,160
Boss Wen.

96
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:25,519
About that matter from last time...

97
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,160
Let's go.

98
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,120
Let's talk over there.

99
00:04:28,439 --> 00:04:29,279
We'll talk over there.

100
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,560
Brother,

101
00:04:33,759 --> 00:04:35,279
try our soy sauce duck.

102
00:04:35,319 --> 00:04:36,240
It's delicious.

103
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:37,120
Let me tell you,

104
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,639
once you eat our food,

105
00:04:38,639 --> 00:04:40,079
drink our liquor,

106
00:04:40,199 --> 00:04:41,720
and make friends here,

107
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,079
you won't want to go home.

108
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,480
Then you marry a local wife,

109
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:47,360
and your life will be fantastic.

110
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:49,600
Really.

111
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,680
Give it a try.

112
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:52,279
No worries.

113
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:53,079
Eat up, eat up.

114
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:54,279
Sorry to bother you, Brother Wu.

115
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,319
I have a favor to ask.

116
00:04:56,399 --> 00:04:56,959
Go ahead.

117
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,040
I have a great-aunt.

118
00:04:58,519 --> 00:04:59,399
She's quite old.

119
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,279
My dad said

120
00:05:00,279 --> 00:05:01,360
she used to live in

121
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,600
Zhangzhou.

122
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,199
We lost touch after a few moves.

123
00:05:05,959 --> 00:05:07,680
Some say she went to Pingtan County.

124
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,959
Others say

125
00:05:09,279 --> 00:05:11,040
she might be in Yongtai County,

126
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,279
in one of its villages or towns.

127
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,600
What's her name?

128
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,560
Lin Zhaodi.

129
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,639
Lin Zhaodi.

130
00:05:15,759 --> 00:05:16,560
Lin, as in "two woods."

131
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:18,920
Let me tell you,

132
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,079
Yongtai is my hometown.

133
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,519
The police there are good friends of mine.

134
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,480
I'll look into it for you right away.

135
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,160
Come.

136
00:05:27,639 --> 00:05:28,240
Brother Wu,

137
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,439
I'll cover the bill at Brother Wen's tonight.

138
00:05:31,879 --> 00:05:33,360
You're too kind, really.

139
00:05:34,759 --> 00:05:35,360
Boss Ding.

140
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,360
Boss Ding.

141
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:39,560
Deputy Mayor Xie sent you

142
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,800
the materials on the preferential policies.

143
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,839
Did you receive them?

144
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:42,839
I don't know what materials you mean.

145
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,279
No, it's very simple.

146
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,720
We're drinking today, no business talk.

147
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:47,399
Come on.

148
00:05:47,399 --> 00:05:48,519
Come on. Cheers!

149
00:06:04,519 --> 00:06:05,519
I'm home.

150
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,800
The Mid-Autumn Festival is still days away.

151
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,079
Why did you buy fish again?

152
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,199
And such an expensive one, too.

153
00:06:11,199 --> 00:06:12,040
Are you making offerings?

154
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:13,759
I didn't buy any fish.

155
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,399
Xiao'ou must have brought it.

156
00:06:16,639 --> 00:06:18,519
Your nephew got stuck with a wife like that.

157
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,360
She wouldn't even give away a single scallion,

158
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,639
let alone bring me a fish.

159
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,360
Out of the four Cao brothers,

160
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,680
Cao Xiao'ou is the only heir.

161
00:06:28,439 --> 00:06:30,360
You treat him like your own son,

162
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,839
but he might not see you as a father.

163
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,160
If he really brought this fish,

164
00:06:35,319 --> 00:06:37,240
I'll walk out of here on my hands.

165
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,519
What's wrong?

166
00:06:54,319 --> 00:06:55,079
What is it?

167
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:58,600
Look.

168
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,360
Even if I played the lottery,

169
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,920
I wouldn't have luck this good.

170
00:07:04,639 --> 00:07:05,360
Look.

171
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,319
Look at this.

172
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:31,839
Let's be friends.

173
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,720
Why did you buy fish again?

174
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,879
And such an expensive one, too.

175
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:38,959
I didn't buy any fish.

176
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:41,519
This is the disciplinary decision for Engineer Jia.

177
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,120
A severe warning within the Party.

178
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,519
Probation at the institute.

179
00:07:44,639 --> 00:07:45,800
Let this be a constant warning.

180
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:47,680
How have you been sleeping?

181
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,519
Not so good lately.

182
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,439
I either can't fall asleep,

183
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,680
or I can't wake up.

184
00:07:53,399 --> 00:07:54,040
And I'm always exhausted.

185
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,120
Hello, I need to make a call.

186
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,040
Okay.

187
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,720
I'm dialing 110.

188
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,200
Yes, I need to report a crime.

189
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,720
It's hard to explain in a few words.

190
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,000
I'd like to

191
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,080
talk to you in person.

192
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,080
Right now, I'm at

193
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,159
the gate of the Institute 761 dorms.

194
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,600
I'll wait for you here.

195
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,440
Okay, goodbye.

196
00:08:50,679 --> 00:08:51,279
Thank you.

197
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:15,200
Take out your ID and driver's license first.

198
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,120
Hand them over.

199
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,080
How were you driving?

200
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:19,759
I'm asking you,

201
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,799
how are you going to explain this to their family?

202
00:09:23,039 --> 00:09:24,639
I didn't mean to.

203
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,159
What do you do for a living?

204
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,240
Delivery.

205
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,200
Have you been drinking?

206
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,159
How fast were you going just now?

207
00:09:33,159 --> 00:09:34,759
Who called the police just now?

208
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,120
Me, me!

209
00:09:40,519 --> 00:09:41,159
Oh, it's you.

210
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:42,200
What happened here?

211
00:09:45,799 --> 00:09:47,320
Someone on a bike hit me.

212
00:09:47,519 --> 00:09:48,759
And conned me out of a burger.

213
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,519
So I called the police.

214
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,240
I had just hung up,

215
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,879
and this car crashed into the newsstand.

216
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:54,559
Yes, yes.

217
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:55,879
I saw it all.

218
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,240
Scared the hell out of me.

219
00:09:57,799 --> 00:09:59,399
Come to the station to give a statement.

220
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,440
A VIP's arrival always brings a storm.

221
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,279
Boss Ding, don't be in such a hurry to leave.

222
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:06,679
Our meeting room is right next door.

223
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:08,039
Let's have a good talk, okay?

224
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,440
Deputy Mayor Xie will be here soon too.

225
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:09,840
Really.

226
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,480
How about this,

227
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,799
leave an address, and just mail it.

228
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,200
Let's not drag this out today, okay?

229
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,600
I've had things mailed before.

230
00:10:15,159 --> 00:10:16,279
Boss Ding. Boss Ding.

231
00:10:16,279 --> 00:10:17,759
Boss Ding, please don't rush off.

232
00:10:17,759 --> 00:10:18,360
Don't leave yet.

233
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,399
Let's sit down and talk.

234
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:21,159
You're already here, Boss Ding.

235
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:21,919
If you leave right now,

236
00:10:21,919 --> 00:10:23,679
I won't be able to explain this to Deputy Mayor Xie.

237
00:10:23,679 --> 00:10:24,399
Boss Ding,

238
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:26,559
our current policies are really excellent.

239
00:10:26,559 --> 00:10:27,639
Just mail it to me.

240
00:10:27,639 --> 00:10:28,320
I'll receive it.

241
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,120
No, wait.

242
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,919
Boss Ding! Boss Ding!

243
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,480
This Wu Jinhe,

244
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,519
is so stubborn.

245
00:10:35,879 --> 00:10:38,080
Officials in the mainland don't have it easy either.

246
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:41,480
Director Wu.

247
00:10:41,639 --> 00:10:43,240
I believe I have the right to resign.

248
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,600
I am the Director.

249
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,080
You want to resign?

250
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,159
Request denied.

251
00:10:47,159 --> 00:10:48,240
It's my right.

252
00:10:50,919 --> 00:10:53,399
This time, regarding the investigation of this photographer,

253
00:10:53,399 --> 00:10:55,240
Chief Wei wants to borrow you for the case.

254
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,600
It's true that Division 2

255
00:10:56,679 --> 00:10:57,759
doesn't have any young women.

256
00:10:58,039 --> 00:10:59,279
To investigate a wedding photo studio,

257
00:10:59,279 --> 00:11:01,360
there has to be a bride, right?

258
00:11:01,799 --> 00:11:03,200
I think I have this right.

259
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,360
I'll grant you a privilege.

260
00:11:04,639 --> 00:11:06,279
You have the right to look through the whole bureau

261
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,759
and pick a fake groom you're satisfied with.

262
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,879
This time,

263
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,159
the mission isn't too difficult.

264
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,480
Go and get some experience.

265
00:11:13,799 --> 00:11:15,360
And bring back a real spy.

266
00:11:15,919 --> 00:11:18,080
We'll talk about the rest later.

267
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,200
He Chunxiao.

268
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:28,120
Why him?

269
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,120
If we pretend he's my fiancé,

270
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,240
compared to the others,

271
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,480
I can act the part more convincingly.

272
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,360
He doesn't talk much.

273
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:35,600
And because no matter what I say, he'll listen.

274
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,240
If I had to get married today,

275
00:11:37,519 --> 00:11:38,720
I'd choose someone like him.

276
00:11:48,799 --> 00:11:49,440
Brother Qi

277
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:56,639
He Chunxiao.

278
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:57,799
Do you need something?

279
00:11:59,399 --> 00:12:01,200
I've been temporarily transferred back to Division Two.

280
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,039
We're teaming up in groups

281
00:12:02,039 --> 00:12:03,440
to look for someone at Wedding Photo Studio Street.

282
00:12:03,519 --> 00:12:04,519
Why don't you partner with me?

283
00:12:04,919 --> 00:12:06,519
You should probably find someone else.

284
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,399
Do you think I'm not up to it?

285
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:09,440
No.

286
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,360
Since you've already decided to resign,

287
00:12:11,519 --> 00:12:13,120
and State Security is a disciplined force...

288
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,279
You're only here on temporary secondment.

289
00:12:14,279 --> 00:12:15,519
The less we know about each other, the better.

290
00:12:15,519 --> 00:12:16,399
Don't you think?

291
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:24,840
Come in.

292
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:28,120
I thought about it.

293
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,440
It should still be Huadong.

294
00:12:29,639 --> 00:12:31,279
Close the door. Come in and talk.

295
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,759
Following normal logic,

296
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:37,600
if I were to find someone to marry,

297
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,600
it would definitely be an outstanding student like Huadong.

298
00:12:39,799 --> 00:12:41,679
In case I run into someone I know on the street,

299
00:12:41,679 --> 00:12:43,440
this makes a lot more sense.

300
00:12:43,919 --> 00:12:45,679
How could I ever marry someone like He Chunxiao?

301
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,519
Marriage is a big deal.

302
00:12:52,759 --> 00:12:53,679
It's your call.

303
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:55,600
Mr. Li!

304
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,240
It's me, Wu Jinhe.

305
00:12:57,799 --> 00:12:58,559
Yes, yes, yes.

306
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:01,000
Last time, you mentioned investing in...

307
00:13:03,799 --> 00:13:05,360
Such a big incident happened in your family?

308
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:06,919
I'm sorry, so sorry.

309
00:13:06,919 --> 00:13:07,679
Sorry to bother you.

310
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,279
It's me!

311
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,919
Wu Jinhe!

312
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,519
We just met earlier.

313
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:19,240
Brother!

314
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,559
So, here's the situation.

315
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,559
About your great-aunt...

316
00:13:21,559 --> 00:13:23,039
I've already made arrangements for you.

317
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,399
The police in Yongtai County and Pingtan,

318
00:13:25,399 --> 00:13:27,360
as well as Civil Affairs, are already looking into it.

319
00:13:27,799 --> 00:13:29,399
Are your friends from Wo Aoma

320
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,799
still with you?

321
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,559
They all left?

322
00:13:33,519 --> 00:13:34,639
That's fine, no worries.

323
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,639
Since they left, let's hang out!

324
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:38,919
Right, right. Where are you?

325
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:39,840
I'll be right there!

326
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,639
Let's add another dish!

327
00:13:48,159 --> 00:13:48,960
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

328
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,399
Brother Wen, let me be honest.

329
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,080
I might be average in other things,

330
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,879
but when I do things,

331
00:13:55,879 --> 00:13:56,919
I live by four words:

332
00:13:57,519 --> 00:13:58,799
Finish what I start.

333
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,519
I told you a long time ago, Old Wu.

334
00:14:01,519 --> 00:14:03,720
Wo Aoma will definitely not invest in you.

335
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,480
At least, not right now.

336
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,360
But you didn't listen.

337
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,840
You ran around everywhere with them,

338
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:08,840
all for nothing.

339
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,480
However, I can invest in you.

340
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,759
Even though I don't have enough money,

341
00:14:14,399 --> 00:14:15,399
let me tell you,

342
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,559
I can introduce a bunch of friends to invest in you.

343
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:19,159
Not to invest in the project,

344
00:14:19,159 --> 00:14:20,559
but to invest in you as a person.

345
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,559
Then I'll invest too!

346
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,480
I'm new here,

347
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,360
and I don't know anyone.

348
00:14:27,759 --> 00:14:29,519
But I trust Brother Wen.

349
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,799
If he invests in you,

350
00:14:30,799 --> 00:14:31,759
I'll invest in you too!

351
00:14:34,679 --> 00:14:36,360
Your great-aunt is my great-aunt!

352
00:14:36,799 --> 00:14:38,120
If I can't find her,

353
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:39,960
I won't come to see you!

354
00:14:40,799 --> 00:14:41,519
Good brother!

355
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,919
He Chunxiao.

356
00:14:55,159 --> 00:14:56,279
Who named you?

357
00:14:56,519 --> 00:14:57,759
I picked it myself.

358
00:14:58,639 --> 00:14:59,480
Why?

359
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,440
My mother's last name is He.

360
00:15:01,639 --> 00:15:03,440
She liked that poem by Meng Haoran.

361
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,720
Hence the name.

362
00:15:16,159 --> 00:15:17,000
Do you know

363
00:15:17,039 --> 00:15:18,639
how many newspaper offices are in the city?

364
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,080
I don't.

365
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:22,080
But the one we're heading to now

366
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,519
is the closest to here,

367
00:15:23,559 --> 00:15:24,799
and also the biggest.

368
00:15:24,799 --> 00:15:26,240
It's just ahead on Hualin Road.

369
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:27,639
As for what you asked about,

370
00:15:27,639 --> 00:15:28,799
we left in such a hurry today

371
00:15:28,799 --> 00:15:30,000
that I didn't have time to check.

372
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:31,480
I'll look into it tonight when we get back.

373
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,039
Get out and push.

374
00:15:59,039 --> 00:15:59,799
Keep pushing.

375
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,799
Brother Qi, can I try first?

376
00:16:24,559 --> 00:16:25,360
What for?

377
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:26,960
Last time...

378
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,399
I didn't have much experience.

379
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:29,879
I didn't pass the review.

380
00:16:29,879 --> 00:16:30,879
I want to try again.

381
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:31,960
Wait, you didn't pass last time.

382
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,159
You think you'll pass this time?

383
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,159
Please, let me try again.

384
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:48,960
Just let me in.

385
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:49,639
You step outside first.

386
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,320
Our office doesn't allow unauthorized entry.

387
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,879
Go ask at some other office.

388
00:16:53,759 --> 00:16:54,480
Police, we're on a case.

389
00:16:56,279 --> 00:16:57,039
Hello, officers.

390
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:57,799
A couple days ago,

391
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,240
there was a street scam.

392
00:16:59,559 --> 00:17:01,759
The victims were all local residents.

393
00:17:01,919 --> 00:17:03,279
There was an eyewitness at the scene.

394
00:17:03,279 --> 00:17:04,640
Based on our information,

395
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,400
this witness

396
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,759
is highly likely a journalist from here.

397
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:08,359
How long have you worked here?

398
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,920
For about seven or eight years.

399
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,200
Then with everyone coming and going every day,

400
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,400
you must be pretty familiar with them, right?

401
00:17:12,559 --> 00:17:13,440
Absolutely.

402
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,920
Then tell us about them.

403
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,359
Let's start with the oldest ones,

404
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:17,880
the senior staff members.

405
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,319
How about I just take you

406
00:17:20,319 --> 00:17:21,759
to their photography department director?

407
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:22,839
Sure.

408
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:24,720
Then follow me.

409
00:17:24,799 --> 00:17:27,359
You need to learn how to use your tools.

410
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,720
No one will believe you on words alone.

411
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,960
When Jinlan went to the train station

412
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:34,079
to check the records before,

413
00:17:34,079 --> 00:17:35,039
she lied.

414
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,519
What happened after?

415
00:17:36,799 --> 00:17:38,039
Isn't that against the rules?

416
00:17:38,279 --> 00:17:39,759
It is. Of course it is.

417
00:17:40,119 --> 00:17:41,319
She'll be disciplined accordingly.

418
00:17:42,319 --> 00:17:43,400
Are you going to report her?

419
00:17:43,519 --> 00:17:44,519
That's not what I meant.

420
00:17:44,519 --> 00:17:45,359
I wanted to ask,

421
00:17:45,559 --> 00:17:47,160
if we need to get something done,

422
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:48,400
but it's against regulations,

423
00:17:48,599 --> 00:17:49,759
like trailing a suspect,

424
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,960
and the person we're investigating

425
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:53,839
goes to places we can't get into,

426
00:17:54,039 --> 00:17:55,759
when regulations clash with the case,

427
00:17:55,759 --> 00:17:56,559
how do we choose?

428
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,880
Do you always like asking questions like this?

429
00:17:59,079 --> 00:18:00,400
Doesn't Wu Jiali find you annoying?

430
00:18:00,759 --> 00:18:02,000
Instructor Wu told us

431
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:04,279
you're the best investigator in our division.

432
00:18:04,279 --> 00:18:05,839
I'm lucky to be partnered with you.

433
00:18:05,839 --> 00:18:07,400
He told me to learn from you

434
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,319
and ask questions when I have them.

435
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,319
He also said

436
00:18:09,319 --> 00:18:10,440
that you're a really nice person,

437
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,480
always answering every question.

438
00:18:12,079 --> 00:18:14,599
Bullshit. The most patient one is Old Wei.

439
00:18:15,119 --> 00:18:17,119
Your Chief Wei loves teaching students the most.

440
00:18:17,119 --> 00:18:18,680
You should ask him about these things.

441
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,079
Or suppose we are now going

442
00:18:21,079 --> 00:18:22,519
to investigate someone for a scam,

443
00:18:22,519 --> 00:18:23,200
which tactics can we use

444
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,119
and which can't we?

445
00:18:24,119 --> 00:18:25,079
If you ask me that,

446
00:18:25,079 --> 00:18:26,839
I can only tell you it's not allowed.

447
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,400
But then you won't solve the case.

448
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,759
Many things don't have a correct answer.

449
00:18:31,839 --> 00:18:33,279
You have to find it yourself.

450
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,720
Stop staring at me like an idiot.

451
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,119
Let me ask you.

452
00:18:37,119 --> 00:18:39,319
If a spy near his target

453
00:18:39,319 --> 00:18:40,799
opens up a nightclub to serve as

454
00:18:40,799 --> 00:18:43,000
a safe house and transit station,

455
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,839
with the boss acting as a lookout,

456
00:18:45,119 --> 00:18:46,920
doing business while gathering intel,

457
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,920
would you go in?

458
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,720
If the superiors agree,

459
00:18:49,799 --> 00:18:50,839
I would go in.

460
00:18:51,359 --> 00:18:53,119
That's why students like you and Huadong,

461
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,279
if I were the boss,

462
00:18:54,279 --> 00:18:55,960
I'd assign you all to desk jobs.

463
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,359
What's one plus one?

464
00:18:57,359 --> 00:18:58,759
Do you even need to ask?

465
00:18:58,839 --> 00:18:59,799
In our line of work,

466
00:18:59,799 --> 00:19:01,319
we have to blend in wherever we go.

467
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:02,599
Listen to me.

468
00:19:02,759 --> 00:19:04,599
Just look around and get a feel for it.

469
00:19:04,599 --> 00:19:05,599
Then request a transfer when you get back.

470
00:19:05,599 --> 00:19:06,799
You're not cut out for intelligence work.

471
00:19:07,039 --> 00:19:09,480
No. Then who is cut out for it?

472
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,240
I can smell it.

473
00:19:11,519 --> 00:19:13,160
Real talents have a certain scent to them.

474
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,640
Your scent is too faint.

475
00:19:14,839 --> 00:19:16,039
Didn't Old Wei ever tell you?

476
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:17,640
You were originally assigned to Division Three.

477
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:18,960
Because he couldn't grab anyone better

478
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,839
and was short-staffed, he brought you over.

479
00:19:21,039 --> 00:19:22,359
If you were a real talent,

480
00:19:22,359 --> 00:19:23,359
would Division Three let you go?

481
00:19:23,599 --> 00:19:25,079
Then why did you choose me?

482
00:19:27,079 --> 00:19:28,240
There are only two pills in the bowl.

483
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,279
Do I have a choice?

484
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:31,519
Actually, Huadong is much more capable than you.

485
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,000
But he annoys me.

486
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,319
Don't people who are full of themselves annoy you?

487
00:19:39,039 --> 00:19:41,119
Hurry up. We still have a few more places to check.

488
00:19:59,119 --> 00:20:00,079
So many shops.

489
00:20:00,279 --> 00:20:01,559
We have to check every single one.

490
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,359
Can we finish them all today?

491
00:20:03,519 --> 00:20:05,240
If you ask me how long it'll take to find someone,

492
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:07,079
I'd just bet on having the best luck.

493
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,680
It's the same for everything else.

494
00:20:08,839 --> 00:20:11,000
If you think like that, it won't seem so hard.

495
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,039
Makes sense.

496
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,400
Valuable life experience, free of charge.

497
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:14,880
Thanks.

498
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:15,440
Newlyweds,

499
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,240
please come this way.

500
00:20:16,359 --> 00:20:17,039
Right over here.

501
00:20:22,839 --> 00:20:23,680
Let's go.

502
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:28,839
You don't act like my fiancé.

503
00:20:29,039 --> 00:20:30,200
Do you think the two of us

504
00:20:30,279 --> 00:20:32,079
look like we're about to get married?

505
00:20:36,359 --> 00:20:39,000
Then how should an engaged couple act?

506
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,519
See what I mean?

507
00:20:42,519 --> 00:20:44,519
I told you this movie was amazing.

508
00:20:44,839 --> 00:20:45,680
Nonsense.

509
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:48,960
Thank you, honey.

510
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:49,680
Don't mention it.

511
00:21:00,319 --> 00:21:01,640
I know what to do.

512
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,519
Let's go. What are you waiting for?

513
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,680
Based on my observation,

514
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:10,759
couples truly getting married

515
00:21:10,759 --> 00:21:12,039
are different from those just dating.

516
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,240
There are just three points.

517
00:21:14,759 --> 00:21:16,440
Holding hands is like carrying a bag.

518
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,960
It's natural. You forget you're holding someone's hand.

519
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:21,319
Walking is like a shadow following the feet.

520
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,279
Where you go, they follow.

521
00:21:23,279 --> 00:21:24,359
No need to say a word.

522
00:21:24,559 --> 00:21:25,880
Kissing is like blinking.

523
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,160
A conditioned reflex.

524
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,640
You don't need to think about it.

525
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:29,839
Hello.

526
00:21:29,839 --> 00:21:31,119
ID photos or wedding portraits?

527
00:21:31,319 --> 00:21:32,079
Wedding portraits.

528
00:21:32,279 --> 00:21:33,519
Can we look at the wedding dresses first?

529
00:21:34,079 --> 00:21:35,680
We only have what's in the frames on the wall.

530
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,559
If it's not there, we don't have it.

531
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:42,599
Miss.

532
00:21:43,039 --> 00:21:44,279
Are you reading *Wangfu Ya*?

533
00:21:45,119 --> 00:21:46,079
You're reading it too?

534
00:21:46,079 --> 00:21:47,039
But I haven't finished it yet.

535
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:48,960
I wonder what happened to that girl later.

536
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:49,960
I haven't finished it either.

537
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,440
That's why I'm rushing to read it.

538
00:21:51,559 --> 00:21:52,880
Have you seen the TV series?

539
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,039
It just premiered a couple of days ago.

540
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,759
There's a TV series already?

541
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,839
Which channel is it on?

542
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,480
On...

543
00:21:59,279 --> 00:22:00,400
Which channel was it again?

544
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,079
Let me think.

545
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,480
Which channel was it again?

546
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,480
The one we always watch.

547
00:22:06,519 --> 00:22:06,880
Miss,

548
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,640
Can I talk to the photographer first?

549
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:09,519
Let him keep thinking.

550
00:22:09,519 --> 00:22:11,240
Second floor. Go up by yourself.

551
00:22:12,519 --> 00:22:13,640
Young man, come here.

552
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:14,559
Which channel is it on?

553
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:29,039
Wasted most of the day for nothing.

554
00:22:29,359 --> 00:22:31,000
Does this happen often?

555
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:33,160
Not usually. When you weren't with me,

556
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,599
I usually found them on the first try.

557
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:41,359
You think it's hard after just one day?

558
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,640
Failing to catch someone for ten or twenty years,

559
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:44,680
happens in every division.

560
00:22:47,319 --> 00:22:49,279
I try to advise you, but you don't appreciate it.

561
00:22:52,799 --> 00:22:54,079
So where do we go next?

562
00:23:02,039 --> 00:23:03,279
